    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d134">

                <pb facs="0451" n="1081" sameAs="frus:frus1873p1v2/pg1081"/>

                <head>No. 440.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. <persName corresp="#p_HR1"
                            type="from">Rublee</persName> to Mr. <persName corresp="#p_HF1"
                            type="to">Fish</persName>.</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Berne</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1873-02-20"><hi rendition="#italic">February</hi> 20, 1873</date>.
                        (Received March 15.)</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 124.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to transmit herewith a
                    translation of the material part of an article on the Mermillod affair, which
                    appeared in the Bund of this city on the 18th instant. The Bund is regarded as
                    the semi-official organ of the government, and in defending the expulsion of M.
                    Mermillod, and explaining the motives upon which that measure was based, it
                    doubtless utters the views of the Federal Council. As such a semi-official
                    exposition you may find its article of some interest.</p>
                <p>I have, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed><persName corresp="#p_HR1">HORACE RUBLEE</persName>.</signed>
                </closer>



                <xi:include href="d134-a1.xml" xpointer="d134-a1"/>
            </div>
